# Protections for the signal-underflow variant corpus. Held IDENTICAL across
# every target in this family on purpose: the frame shape, the timer mechanism
# and the command vocabulary are the variables, so a protection difference
# would confound the measurement.
#
# -fstack-protector   LOAD-BEARING, and not as an obstacle: it is what puts the
#                     loop's own control scalars BELOW the array, which is the
#                     only reason the underflow lands somewhere useful. It also
#                     matches the measured target (ancient_interface has a
#                     canary on the vulnerable function). The canary is never
#                     touched by this technique -- the reprogrammed cursor
#                     starts above it.
# -no-pie             fixed gadget/PLT addresses, as in the target
# -O0                 the whole primitive depends on the accumulate loop
#                     reloading its cursor and count from stack slots each
#                     iteration; at higher -O they live in registers and the
#                     target silently stops being in this category
# -lrt                timer_create/timer_settime (glibc < 2.34 keeps them in
#                     librt); harmless on newer glibc
-fstack-protector
-no-pie
-O0
-lrt
# -s                  the measured target is STRIPPED, so the corpus is too:
#                     nothing here may be solved by leaning on a function name
#                     the real challenge does not carry
-s
